Date: Mon, 4 Oct 93 09:56:21 PDT
From: hfinney@shell.portal.com (Hal Finney)
Subject: DIET: Too little fat causes brain damage!

It is important to realize that Brooks' post was a hoax, as he clearly stated.

TOO LITTLE FAT DOES NOT CAUSE BRAIN DAMAGE.

Frankly, I think this was an unfortunate and inappropriate hoax.  I, too,
was taken in by the first few paragraphs.  I have read of studies in the
past which gave VERY TENTATIVE HINTS that suicide rates were higher in
people with very low fat diets.  Brooks' hoax was all too plausible given
this background.

Even though I noticed Brooks' disclaimer at the end of the posting, I
found that I had already integrated the text of the article into my
mental framework, and I had to mentally "catch" myself several times
over the course of the day and remind myself that this new discovery
was not true.  I almost mentioned it to my wife, several times.

If you want to perpetrate a hoax, make it funny, or give it some other
reason for existing.

Hal Finney
